 "preferred_name": "Secured transactions",
 "kind": "knowledge",
 "definition": "The area of commercial law that governs loans and credit backed by collateral in personal property, such as Article 9 of the US Uniform Commercial Code.",
 "description": {
  "text": "A loan or credit transaction where the lender takes a security interest in the borrower's collateral and can foreclose on or repossess it if the borrower defaults. A contract called a security agreement governs it, and in the US Article 9 of the UCC covers personal property.",
